rule c1xx: the three places C1XX's tree does NOT keep the source order of two operands, each moving the operands' FIRST REFERENCES (C2 numbers a symbol at its first reference in reader order): - `i + p` (integer first) is built as `p + i`: add(load p, mul(load i, size)) -- the same IL as `p + i` (expr_build_builtin_binary c1xx!0x10414137); - `i[p]` is built as `p[i]`: index(load p, mul(load i, size)); - a non-member `operator+(a, b)` is a call, and a call's arguments are written LAST first: vb, then va.
cl
